.TH "SVGTEXTPATHELEMENT.METHOD" "3JS" "June 26, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SVGTextPathElement.method \- SVGTextPathElement: method property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]method\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]SVGTextPathElement\f[R] interface represents the method by which
text should be rendered along the path.
.PP
Note that the \f[CR]method.baseVal\f[R] property reflects the
\f[CR]method\f[R] attribute of the given \f[CR]<textPath>\f[R] element,
as an enumerated value.
While \f[CR]method\f[R] is read\-only, you can use
\f[CR]method.baseVal\f[R] to modify the value of the corresponding
attribute.
.PP
In SVG 2, \f[CR]side.method\f[R] also reflects the non\-animated value
of the attribute.
.SH VALUE
An \f[CR]SVGAnimatedEnumeration\f[R] object.
.PP
The following static properties indicate the values that can be returned
from \f[CR]method.baseVal\f[R] (and \f[CR]method.animVal\f[R]):
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_UNKNOWN\f[R] (0)
The type is not one of the predefined types.
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_ALIGN\f[R] (1)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]align\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]SVGTextPathElement.TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_STRETCH\f[R] (2)
Corresponds to the value \f[CR]stretch\f[R].
.PP
Note that \f[CR]baseVal\f[R] cannot be set to \f[CR]0\f[R]
(\f[CR]TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_UNKNOWN\f[R]) or any value other than those
listed above.
\f[CR]animVal\f[R] is read\-only and with throw if you attempt to write
to it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Accessing the \f[CR]method\f[R] property
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]svg\f[R] xmlns=\(dqhttp://www.w3.org/2000/svg\(dq width=\(dq400\(dq height=\(dq200\(dq>
  <\f[B]defs\f[R]>
    <\f[B]path\f[R] id=\(dqmyPath\(dq d=\(dqM10 80 C 40 10, 65 10, 95 80 S 150 150, 180 80\(dq />
  </\f[B]defs\f[R]>
  <\f[B]text\f[R] font\-size=\(dq20\(dq fill=\(dqblue\(dq>
    <\f[B]textPath\f[R] id=\(dqmyTextPath\(dq href=\(dq#myPath\(dq method=\(dqalign\(dq>
      This text follows a path!
    </\f[B]textPath\f[R]>
  </\f[B]text\f[R]>
</\f[B]svg\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] textPath = document.getElementById(\(dqmyTextPath\(dq);

\f[I]// Access the method property\f[R]
console.log(textPath.method.baseVal); \f[I]// Output: 1 (TEXTPATH_METHODTYPE_ALIGN)\f[R]
.EE
